'''Steven Martin''' (born December 24, 1964) is an American former professional [[American football|football]] player who was a [[defensive end]] for the [[Washington Redskins]] of the [[National Football League]] (NFL).<ref>{{cite news | url=https://www.newspapers.com/article/daily-news/176860196/ | title=7 local gridders on NFL rosters | work=[[Bogalusa Daily News|The Daily News]] | date=July 10, 1988 | accessdate=17 July 2025 | author=Byrd, Mike | pages=12A}}</ref> He played [[college football]] for the [[Jackson State Tigers football|Jackson State Tigers]]. He received a gold football the year of [[Super Bowl 50]] for being on the Washington Redskins when they won the Super Bowl.{{Cn|date=May 2025}}

Martin went to [[Varnado High School]] and was the first player from Varnado to make it to the NFL.{{Cn|date=May 2025}}
